# Maison Luminaire — environment configuration
# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
# The path is resolved relative to prisma/schema.prisma.

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root, git-ignored. A RELATIVE `file:` URL is resolved against
# prisma/schema.prisma — exactly like the Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db`
# points at <repo>/db/custom.db for the CLI (migrate/seed), `next build`, and
# the running server alike, regardless of the process working directory.
# (src/lib/db-path.ts implements this resolution; tests/db-path.test.ts
# pins the contract.)
# NOTE — environment precedence: an ambient DATABASE_URL process variable
# beats this file (standard dotenv rule). Sandboxed/managed shells that
# export an absolute DATABASE_URL pointing outside the repo would silently
# relocate the dev database; the wrapped dev scripts (scripts/with-repo-db.ts
# → dev/build/start/db:push/db:seed/db:migrate/db:reset) defend against that
# by resolving THIS file's value first for dev flows. Production keeps
# env-var precedence (12-factor).
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is still recommended — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
# To use PostgreSQL:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string
#   3. bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
# PostgreSQL example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/maison_luminaire

# ---- Site ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin — resolves the app's `metadataBase` (canonical
# metadata URLs) via src/lib/site.ts AND the sitemap.xml/robots.txt locs
# (src/lib/seo.ts); falls back to http://localhost:3000 when unset or
# malformed. Set to the deployed URL in production.
# NOTE — BUILD-TIME BAKING: Next inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables into the
# server bundles at build time, so the canonical origin (canonical URLs +
# sitemap/robots) is fixed by the value present when `next build` runs.
# Changing it at runtime does NOT change the served locs — set it in .env
# (or the build environment) BEFORE building the deployment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Session signing secret for HMAC cookie auth.
# REQUIRED in production: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Falls back to an insecure dev-only constant when unset.
AUTH_SECRET=""

# ---- Seed -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo login password for the seeded user (sepnetflix2023@outlook.com).
# Optional — falls back to the documented demo credential.
# DEMO_USER_PASSWORD=""
